# Negative-control mutant — the row status is a translated-badge-ready `meta`
# group, not a bare `{ code }` (G2, R38 item 9)
#
# Scenario it must flip: a contract's `meta` carries exactly one truthy flag —
#   the one matching its own `status.code` — so the `TableCellBadges` renderer
#   (`playgrounds/labs-nuxt/.../cells/TableCellBadges.vue:31-37`, one badge per
#   truthy flag of a scoped object) can draw a translated status badge, the
#   same `meta` idiom `tickets.mappers.ts` publishes for its own status.
# Mutation: `mapContractMeta` ignores the contract's OWN `status.code` and
#   returns every flag `false` — no badge is ever true, so a hand sees a
#   contract with no status at all.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.mappers.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.mappers.ts
